    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Trees are very important. They provide shelter for animals and add beauty to our surroundings. They use sunlight to convert water and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "carbon dioxide",
            "zh": "二氧化碳"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " into the oxygen we breathe. Why not plant some trees to make your neighbourhood greener? This guide will show you how."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Planting trees"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{1} Before carrying "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "seedlings",
            "zh": "幼苗"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to your site, place them in a bucket "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "lined",
            "ref": "v-line"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with wet paper towels to keep their roots "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "moist"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{2} Dig a hole deep enough for the seedling’s whole root system."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{3} Using your hands, cover the seedling with soil. All roots should be buried. The seedling should stand "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "upright",
            "ref": "v-upright"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{4} "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "Pack",
            "ref": "v-pack"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the dirt tightly around the seedling."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Setting weed mats in place"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Weedy plants can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "compete",
            "ref": "v-compete"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with a tree for water and nutrients in the soil before a tree takes root. Weed mats prevent their growth by blocking sunlight. The mats also keep the soil moist."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{1} Weed mats have a “shiny” side and a “rough” side. The shiny side should always face up."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{2} Gently guide the plant through the hole in the centre of the mat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "{3} Fold under each corner of the mat. Drive a nail into each corner. The mat should be flat against the ground."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Watering trees"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After you have finished planting your trees, water them until the surrounding soil is moist. To decide whether you need to water your trees, you can dig an eight-centimetre-deep hole near one of them. If the soil in the hole is dry, you should water the trees."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
